  "record": {
    "read_status": "full",
    "file_problem": "none",
    "relation": "cites_only",
    "tranche": "T6",
    "tranche_reason": "The study uses linear activation probes and activation addition to detect and steer empathy. It does not test superposition, feature overlap, capacity competition, or SAE feature recovery.",
    "gate_note": "The paper reports empirical results about empathy directions in LLM activations, but does not measure whether more features than dimensions are represented, whether features overlap or are nearly orthogonal, or whether features are distributed across neurons. No claim version is tested. Rows below record related linear-direction findings; they do not establish superposition.",
    "test_reason": "The study extracts mean-difference empathy probes and steers with them in three LLMs. It cites Toy Models of Superposition only as a source for the linear representation hypothesis. It does not test superposition, feature overlap, capacity competition, polysemanticity, SAE features, or feature dimensionality. Its probing results bear on linear representability of one concept, which is a related but different construct. T6 fits better than T4: the study neither uses superposition as a tool nor tests it.",
    "authors_conclusion": "Correct. The authors conclude that empathy is linearly detectable within each model and is independent of safety training. Probe directions are model-specific. Steering is model-dependent: Qwen is bidirectional and coherent, while Dolphin is asymmetric and collapses under anti-empathy steering. The authors suggest safety training adds steering robustness. They draw no conclusions about superposition.",
    "recipe": "different",
    "recipe_differences": "The study extracts mean-difference probes from contrastive LLM activations and adds them during generation; it does not use the toy-network superposition method.",
    "method_sensitivity": "Probe AUROC varies by layer, with the best layer differing by model. Probe agreement across models is weak.",
    "fits_no_version": [
      {
        "finding": "Mean-difference empathy probes separate contrastive empathic and non-empathic text at AUROC 0.79–1.00 across layers in Phi-3, Qwen2.5-7B and Dolphin-Llama-3.1-8B. Performance peaks in middle layers.",
        "proposed_claim": "A contrastively prompted socio-emotional concept is linearly decodable from LLM activations, with layer-dependent probe accuracy.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r1",
          "r2",
          "r3",
          "r4",
          "r5",
          "r6",
          "r7",
          "r8",
          "r9",
          "r10",
          "r11",
          "r12",
          "r13",
          "r14",
          "r15"
        ]
      },
      {
        "finding": "The Phi-3 probe correlates with human empathy scores (r=0.71, N=12). Probes from the other models scoring the same Phi-3 completions agree weakly (r=−0.06, 0.18).",
        "proposed_claim": "Within-model linear concept probes track behaviour, but the directions are model-specific.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r18",
          "r19",
          "r20"
        ]
      },
      {
        "finding": "Phi-3 probe AUROC stays at 1.0 after keyword removal, and random directions average AUROC 0.50.",
        "proposed_claim": "Linear empathy detection is not explained by lexical cues or arbitrary directions.",
        "row_ids": [
          "r16",
          "r17"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "controls": "y",
    "capability_check": "y",
    "uncertainty_reported": "y",
    "code_released": "https://github.com/juancadile/empathy-probes",
    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The evidence is based on 15 held-out contrastive pairs for probe validation and 12 synthetic completions for behavioral correlation. The paper itself notes limited model diversity, including only one uncensored model; its coherence checks use simple heuristics. These limitations concern its empathy-probe results, which do not test the catalog claim.",
    "rows_left_out": "Steering success-rate and coherence results were not included: they evaluate the paper's empathy-steering method rather than superposition, feature overlap, or a claim version. The paper reports scenario-specific values in Table 3 and discusses further layer/scenario patterns in Figures 6–9.",
    "untested": [
      {
