        "parts": "All: no toy models, no feature-count vs dimension comparison, no sparsity transition, no geometry."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "All: no neuron-level polysemanticity or capacity analysis."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "All."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "No measure of feature spread across neurons and no SAE. Linear probe separability of one concept does not bear on this version."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "All: no SAE features."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "The study assumes a single 1-D empathy direction. It does not compare this with multi-dimensional features."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [],
    "verdict_notes": "Toy Models of Superposition is cited only as support for the linear representation hypothesis. The evidence base is small: 15 test pairs and 12 completions. The prompts explicitly instruct empathic or non-empathic behaviour, so the contrast is prompt-induced. Steering results were correctly left out. No verdicts are given because no claim version is tested."
  },
